//! Per-series LG webOS TV caprichios, model years 2018 (webOS TV 4.0) to 2026.
//!
//! Each series below is its own caprichio, a module with contract
//! `goya.platform.webos.<slug>.v1`, generated by [`crate::webos_series!`].
//! Columns: slug, name, decoder code, model year, family, shipped platform,
//! upgrade ceiling. The engine for each platform is in
//! [`crate::webos_engine_caprichio::PLATFORMS`].
//!
//! The shipped platform follows from the model year: LG ships one webOS
//! release per year across its whole range. A series missing from this
//! list still resolves by year through
//! [`crate::webos_engine_caprichio::decode_model`]; listing it only adds the
//! per-series contract and the upgrade ceiling.
//!
//! Upgrade ceilings, from LG's Re:New schedule (January 2025):
//! * 2021 StanbyME → webOS 25.
//! * 2022 OLED, 8K QNED (QNED95/99) and StanbyME Go → webOS 25.
//! * 2023 and 2024 OLED, QNED and LCD → webOS 25.
//!
//! The ceiling is raised to webOS 26 only where a TV of that series was
//! observed reporting 11.x: C3 and G3 (2023), and G5 (2025). Every other
//! series has a ceiling equal to its shipped platform.
//!
//! 2026 OLED rows are catalogued, but the decoder refuses `OLED..6..` model
//! numbers, because the year digit 6 is shared with the 2016 range.

